# Plan: Agentic Workflow Kit + GlyphNotif for Nothing Phone (3)

## Context

You want two things.

**1. A Nothing Phone (3) app (`C:\Users\guilh\git\nothingnotif`, empty, not yet a git repo).** For each selected app, rules match notifications by title, keywords or sender ("emitter"), and each match shows a chosen glyph on the 25×25 Glyph Matrix on the back of the phone.
- Glyphs are drawn by hand, or imported from a photo.
- A photo converter produces a sparse glyph with very few lit points. It offers 3 auto-tuned options and sliders, with a live preview on the back of the phone.

**2. A generic, reusable agentic-programming workflow kit.** It must not be tied to Kotlin or to Claude. It should work in any language and with any LLM or agent tool. It includes full adapters for Claude Code and for the most popular open-source agent CLIs as of September 2026.

**Both are developed with the same process.** Specs are written first, then tests. Tests are committed and frozen once you have verified them. Implementation iterates until all tests pass. Tests never change without your agreement. Token usage must stay low without hurting code quality or speed much.

## Decisions you made

| Topic | Decision |
|---|---|
| Kit location | A sibling repo, `C:\Users\guilh\git\agentic-workflow-kit`. nothingnotif is **installed from it**, so it is the kit's first real user. |
| Adapters | **Full** adapters for Claude Code + the top open-source agent CLIs (below) |
| First deliverable for nothingnotif | Workflow files + an Android multi-module skeleton that builds green. No feature code. |
| Gates | **You approve every gate** (spec approved → tests approved → freeze) |
| Frozen tests | Edits are **hard-blocked**. Only you unfreeze, by running a command yourself, and every unfreeze is logged. |

## Research findings (condensed)

**Glyph Matrix Developer Kit** (`Nothing-Developer-Programme/GlyphMatrix-Developer-Kit`):
- **Library and permission:** `glyph-matrix-sdk-2.0.aar` and the permission `com.nothing.ketchum.permission.ENABLE`.
- **Device:** Phone (3) is `Glyph.DEVICE_23112`. Its 25×25 grid holds **489 physical LEDs laid out in a circle**.
- **App display:** an app pushes a frame with `GlyphMatrixManager.init / register / setAppMatrixFrame(int[]|GlyphMatrixFrame) / closeAppMatrix`. This requires system version ≥ 20250801.
- **Display priority:** Glyph Toys take priority over apps, and the Glyph Button overrides app content.
- **Not documented** (the hardware spike will answer these):
  - the value range of raw frames;
  - whether frames display when the screen is off or locked, or when pushed from a background `NotificationListenerService`;
  - the refresh rate;
  - interaction with the phone's own glyph notifications.

**Instruction and skill standards:**
- **AGENTS.md** is the cross-tool instruction file standard (Linux Foundation AAIF). Claude Code reads it only when there is no CLAUDE.md, or when a CLAUDE.md imports it with `@AGENTS.md`. **The import is the way to avoid duplicated tokens.**
- **Agent Skills** (`SKILL.md`, agentskills.io) is an open standard with 30+ supporting tools. Skills load progressively: about 30–50 tokens per skill at startup, and the full body only when used.

**Top open-source agent CLIs (Aug–Sep 2026, by stars):**

| Agent | Stars | License | What it supports |
|---|---|---|---|
| DeepSeek Harness | ~203k | MIT | Everything is a plugin. Reads AGENTS.md, falling back to CLAUDE.md. Its hook-bridge plugins run existing Claude Code / Codex `hooks.json`. |
| OpenCode | ~202k | MIT | `.opencode/plugins/` with a `tool.execute.before` hook (throwing an error blocks the call) and a `session.idle` event. Provider-agnostic, including local models. |
| Codex CLI | ~119k | Apache-2.0 | `.codex/hooks.json` with a **schema almost identical to Claude Code's**: PreToolUse/Stop, exit code 2 or `permissionDecision: deny`. File edits go through `apply_patch`. Project hooks need a trust step. Skills live in `.agents/skills`. |
| Pi | ~98k | MIT | A minimal harness with a system prompt under 1k tokens, lazily loaded skills, and extensions |

- Gemini CLI was **retired on 18 June 2026**. Its successor, Antigravity CLI, is closed source, and its open-source fork lives on as Qwen Code. Aider has been inactive since May 2026.
- Goose, Cline, OpenHands and Crush are covered by the tool-neutral baseline only.

**Claude Code practice:**
- CLAUDE.md under 200 lines; path-scoped `.claude/rules/`; skills for workflows.
- Hooks give deterministic gates. Subagents isolate verbose work.
- Prompt-cache hygiene, model and effort routing, and hooks that filter command output before the agent reads it.

**Spec-driven development:** Spec Kit / Kiro style. One folder per feature (`spec.md`/`plan.md`/`tasks.md`), **EARS** requirements with stable IDs, and a constitution of rules that never change.

**Local toolchain (checked):** git 2.48, JDK 17, Python 3.14, Node 22, uv, pwsh 7, adb, Android SDK. Gradle, gh and jq are not installed.

