## Part C: nothingnotif (installed from the kit, `--profile kotlin-gradle --adapters claude-code`)

Other adapters can be added later with a single `agentkit install --adapters …`.

### Project-specific files (added on top of the kit install)

- **AGENTS.md project sections:**
  - product summary;
  - module map and dependency rules (no `android.*` imports in `core:*`);
  - conventions: fakes instead of mocks in core, injected clock and dispatchers, test names start with requirement IDs, ASCII golden 25×25 grids;
  - gotchas: Glyph SDK priority and system version, PowerShell vs bash, CRLF.
- **CLAUDE.md:** `@AGENTS.md` + Claude specifics (model tiers per skill, compaction preferences).
- **`.claude/rules/` (path-scoped):**
  - `kotlin-core.md` (`core/**`);
  - `android.md` (`app/**`, `data/**`, `glyph/**`, including Nothing SDK gotchas);
  - `tests.md`;
  - `specs.md`.
- **Skills:**
  - project skill `device/`: build, install on the Phone (3) over adb, device tests, logcat filtered to our tags.
- **Docs:**
  - `docs/architecture.md`;
  - `docs/hardware/phone3-glyph-matrix.md` (SDK facts + the spike's questions);
  - `docs/adr/0001-native-kotlin-compose`, `0002-pure-kotlin-core`, `0003-agentkit-workflow`.
- **First spec:** `specs/000-product-vision/spec.md`, covering personas, user stories, glossary, v1 scope, what is out of scope (animations, Glyph Museum import, other devices) and the roadmap. It is a **draft for your approval**.
- **Android skeleton:**
  - Gradle wrapper; `settings.gradle.kts`;
  - `gradle/libs.versions.toml` (latest stable AGP, Kotlin, Compose BOM, JUnit 5, Kotest, Robolectric, Roborazzi, Turbine);
  - convention plugins in `build-logic/` (including Spotless/ktlint and Detekt);
  - the 8 modules below as empty shells, with a single no-op app screen.

### Product architecture (target)

Native **Kotlin + Jetpack Compose (Material 3)**, Phone (3) only (minSdk 35), using Hilt and Room. All logic lives in **pure-Kotlin JVM modules**, so tests are fast and need no device.

| Module | Kind | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| `:core:model` | pure | `GlyphFrame` (25×25, 0–255), `Phone3LedMask` (489 LEDs), `Glyph`, `AppProfile`, `Rule`/`Condition`, `GlyphDisplay` interface, ASCII-grid codec |
| `:core:rules` | pure | `NotificationEvent` → `RuleEngine` → `GlyphAction`. Conditions on TITLE / TEXT (keywords) / SENDER / ANY, with operators contains / equals / starts-with / regex. Matching is case- and accent-insensitive. Rules apply by priority, with a default glyph per app. |
| `:core:playback` | pure | Duration, queue, de-duplication, ignoring ongoing and group-summary notifications. Clock and dispatchers are injected. |
| `:core:editor` | pure | Manual editor state machine: pen and brightness brush, eraser, mirror symmetry, shift and rotate, invert, undo/redo |
| `:core:converter` | pure | Photo → sparse glyph pipeline (below) |
| `:data` | Android | Room repositories, JSON backup |
| `:glyph` | Android | Nothing SDK adapter (`GlyphDisplay`), a throttled latest-wins live-preview channel, `FakeGlyphDisplay` (testFixtures), and a no-op implementation for the emulator |
| `:app` | Android | Compose UI, `NotificationListenerService` (title, text, bigText and MessagingStyle sender → `NotificationEvent`), onboarding |

**Converter pipeline:**
1. Decode the image, apply EXIF rotation, and work at about 250 px.
2. Optionally isolate the subject (ML Kit segmentation, behind an interface, with a pure fallback).
3. Fit the image to the circle (pan, zoom, rotate).
4. Tone: luminance, auto-levels, gamma and contrast.
5. Compute an edge map (Sobel).
6. Downsample to 25×25 with area averaging, while keeping edges (edge-aware max).
7. Render in one of three modes:
   - **Silhouette:** Otsu threshold, then fill.
   - **Outline:** thinned 1-LED strokes.
   - **Tonal:** 3–4 brightness levels with error diffusion.
8. Sparsify: remove isolated LEDs, cap the number of lit LEDs at a **point budget**, and keep strokes connected.
9. Apply the LED mask.

The **3 recommendations** are these three modes, each auto-tuned and ranked by a score:
- structural similarity to the area-averaged reference;
- penalties for LED count, noise (number of separate blobs) and an off-centre subject.

**Sliders:** mode, threshold, contrast, gamma, detail, point budget, line thickness, invert, zoom, pan and rotate. Each step has a budget of ≤ 16 ms. The preview mirrors to the back of the phone, throttled.

### Per-feature cycle

The kit skills drive each feature:
1. `/spec` → the spec-reviewer checks it → **you approve**.
2. `/write-tests` → API stubs `TODO("REQ-ID")` + tests that compile and fail → `agentkit trace` → test-auditor review → **you approve**.
3. `/freeze` (only you can trigger it): commit `test(NNN)` + lock.
4. `/implement`: targeted tests → full check → impl-reviewer looks for test-gaming → `feat(NNN)`.

**Test tiers:**
- pure modules: JUnit 5 + Kotest (incl. property tests);
- Android modules: Robolectric + Compose UI tests + Roborazzi;
- flows: Turbine;
- `@DeviceOnly` instrumented tests on the Phone (3), run manually.

### Roadmap

0. **Hardware spike.** This is the only step exempt from TDD. Throwaway code goes in `spikes/`. It answers:
   - the value range of raw frames;
   - whether display works from a background listener and with the screen off or locked;
   - how long a frame persists;
   - the refresh rate;
   - conflicts with the phone's own glyph notifications and with Toys;
   - the exact LED mask.

   If background display turns out to be impossible, I'll come back to you to rescope before going further.
1. `001` model + LED geometry + ASCII golden format
2. `002` display adapter + live preview
3. `003` notification capture
4. `004` rule engine
5. `005` playback
6. `006` persistence and backup
7. `007` manual editor
8. `008` converter pipeline
9. `009` 3 recommendations
10. `010` converter UI with sliders + live preview on the back of the phone
11. `011` app picker and rules UI
12. `012` onboarding and permissions

